{
 "brief": "The Euro-Mediterranean Human Rights Monitor warned that Israel is deliberately dismantling Gaza's transport and shipping infrastructure through systematic destruction of trucks, warehouses operated by logistics companies, and targeting of drivers for arrest, Shehab Wire reported. The group also cited Israeli prevention of truck entry into the enclave as part of the blockade strategy.\n\nThe rights organization characterized these coordinated actions as deliberately pushing Gaza toward renewed famine conditions. By crippling the territory's ability to move goods and maintain supply networks, the blockade threatens food security across the population and disrupts humanitarian aid distribution channels that depend on functional transport systems.",
